1. Make sure you have installed Flask with pip
2. create a .py file with filename of your choice (e.g. fname.py)
3. fill in the fname.py file according to server.py in lab1
4. run the following command in the terminal: 
flask --app fname --debug run

The server is now running locally using port 5000 by default.

5. To connect to the server open a new terminal window and run the following
command: 
curl -X GET -i -w '\n' localhost:5000

